VMA: 32 MB default blocks on large heaps (iOS build).

Minecraft 26.3 creates its VMA allocator with the default block size. VMA
grows blocks 32, 64, 128 MB up to 256 MB, and each block is one Metal
allocation on KosmicKrisp, counted in full against the app's footprint
whatever is used inside it. Measured on the Mac with the Vulkan shim's
accounting: 736 MB allocated for 528 MB of buffers and images in a world
(992 MB on the iPhone, where iOS limits the app to about 3.3 GB). With
32 MB blocks, allocations bigger than 16 MB get memory of their own and the
rest share small blocks: 801 MB allocated for 772 MB used, with the slack
down from 200-450 MB to about 30 MB.

diff --git a/modules/lwjgl/vma/src/main/c/vk_mem_alloc.h b/modules/lwjgl/vma/src/main/c/vk_mem_alloc.h
--- a/modules/lwjgl/vma/src/main/c/vk_mem_alloc.h
+++ b/modules/lwjgl/vma/src/main/c/vk_mem_alloc.h
@@ -3548,7 +3548,9 @@

 #ifndef VMA_DEFAULT_LARGE_HEAP_BLOCK_SIZE
    /// Default size of a block allocated as single VkDeviceMemory from a "large" heap.
-   #define VMA_DEFAULT_LARGE_HEAP_BLOCK_SIZE (256ULL * 1024 * 1024)
+   /* Voxelium (iOS): 32 MB instead of 256 MB, so partly filled blocks don't
+    * hold hundreds of MB of the app's memory (patches/lwjgl/3.4.3-0002). */
+   #define VMA_DEFAULT_LARGE_HEAP_BLOCK_SIZE (32ULL * 1024 * 1024)
 #endif

